🎓 Student Task Manager

A feature-rich, interactive web application built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3. 
Designed specifically for students to manage homework, assignments, exam schedules, and personal goals efficiently.

✨ Features

➕ Task Creation: Add tasks with custom titles, categories, priorities, and due dates.
📊 Live Dashboard Statistics: Dynamic counters displaying Total, Completed, and Pending tasks in real-time.
🏷️ Categorization & Priorities: Tag items by category (Homework, Assignment, Exam, Personal) and assign priority levels (High, Medium, Low).
🚨 Overdue Task Highlighting: Automatic identification and visual highlighting of tasks past their due dates.
🔍 Search & Filter: Search tasks by name, filter by status (All, Completed, Pending), and sort by priority or due date.
🖐️ Drag-and-Drop Reordering: Intuitive HTML5 drag-and-drop mechanics to manually reorder tasks.
💾 Data Persistence: Integrated localStorage ensures your tasks and theme preference persist across browser sessions.
🌙 Dark Mode: Built-in theme switcher supporting light and dark modes with custom CSS variables.
✏️ Edit & Delete: Update task details or remove completed tasks seamlessly.

🛠️ Built With

HTML5: Semantic document structure and native Drag & Drop API.
CSS3: Custom properties (CSS variables), Flexbox, and modern UI transitions.
JavaScript (ES6+): Modular event handling, array methods (filter, sort, reduce), and Web Storage API (localStorage).

🚀 Getting Started

Prerequisites
You need a modern web browser (e.g., Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge) to run this application.

Installation
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/danial-uet/Web-Development-Internship/tree/main/Task%20Manager%20App

Run the app:
Simply open index.html in your web browser.

Alternatively, open the folder in VS Code and run it using the Live Server extension.

📁 Project Structure
student-task-manager/
│
├── index.html     # Application structure and layout
├── style.css      # Custom styling, responsive design, and dark theme
├── script.js      # Main application logic, state management, and DOM handling
└── README.md      # Project documentation
